# Jobs API: runnable browser example

## Use the app origin

Open the live app or your local app, then use the browser console on that same origin. POSTs require the session cookie and same-origin checks; this API is not a cross-origin public SDK.

```js
const created = await fetch('/api/jobs', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    title: 'My verified text task',
    input: 'hello edgeswarm',
    reward: 50
  })
});
if (!created.ok) throw new Error(await created.text());
const job = await created.json();
const processed = await fetch('/api/jobs/' + job.id, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ action: 'process' })
});
const result = await processed.json();
console.log(result.status, result.verdict.checks);
```

The normal process action executes, verifies and settles **demo credits**. SETTLED here does not mean a Solana transaction occurred.

## Inputs and actions

- title: 3–120 characters; input: 1–10,000 characters.
- reward: integer demo credits from 1 to 1,000, not lamports or USDC.
- POST /api/jobs/:id accepts process, execute, verify or settle.
- GET /api/jobs returns the current session's jobs; GET /api/metrics returns its counters.
- POST process with tamper: true intentionally changes output and should result in REJECTED.
- GET /api/jobs/:id/receipt exports evidence without private keys.

For executable assertions and exact current behavior, inspect scripts/smoke.mjs and tests/core.test.mjs in the repository. Never paste code into a browser console from a source you do not trust.
